{
	title: 'inspect: what, scope and fields; session context use',
	spec: `The inspect tool takes three optional arguments: what ('sessions', the default; 'host'; 'models'), scope ('self', the default; 'project'; 'all') and fields (comma-separated names; omitted means every field of that view). A bare inspect() thus describes only the calling session in a few lines; wider scopes are asked for. The schema names every value of what and scope and every field, each in a few words, since a model ignores views a schema does not name (task ed).

sessions: one object per open tab, in tab order. scope 'self' is the caller; 'project' is the tabs sharing the caller's cwd (task 22's project, so scope and tab colors agree); 'all' is every tab. Fields: tab (number), id, name, state (running/idle/paused/asking with phase or reason, as today), model, cwd, color (the project color's name, e.g. cyan; the palette in common/colors.ts gives each of its 8 colors one plain English name), context (the status row's figure from stats.of, e.g. '87k/1000k (9%)'; used only when the window is unknown; 'none' before the first provider response). The caller's row is marked '(you)' after its id.

host: pid, version, started (ISO), uptime, clients (count). scope does not apply. models: as today (default model, then ids by provider); scope and fields do not apply.

Output is plain text. One object prints 'field: value' lines; several print a header line of field names, then one tab-separated line per object. An unknown what, scope or field is an error listing the valid values, so a model learns them on first misuse. No secrets, client addresses or user agents.

Follow-ups extend these views with more fields: who sent the last prompt (client kind), files being edited, client details and all non-secret configuration.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Color names come from rendered sRGB of the palette: p2 (47.5) is the true orange (255,124,0), p3 (87.5) renders amber (243,168,0), though task 22 calls ~/hal's color 3 orange. color is 'none' with a single project, since projects.paint sets no colors then. context reuses stats.of (live round context, else the last turn_end in history) and models.contextWindow."
	],
	needs: ['ed', '1g', '22'],
	foldInto: ['ed']
}
